      "text": "There is **no single 1:1 open-source drop-in replacement** for Pico’s Corvil Analytics. Corvil is a highly specialized platform that combines hardware-accelerated nanosecond timestamping, lossless high-speed packet capture (up to 200 Gbps), built-in decoders for financial protocols (FIX, ITCH, OUCH, SBE), microburst detection, and multi-hop trade lifecycle correlation.\n\nHowever, depending on **which part of Corvil** you are trying to replicate, you can get very close using specialized open-source tools—or by combining a few of them into a stack.\n\n---\n\n### 1. For Financial Protocol (FIX) \u0026 Nanosecond Latency Tracking\nIf you want Corvil’s core trading/HFT latency analytics (measuring order-to-ack delays and hop-by-hop network latency), look at these specialized open-source tools:\n\n* **`ebpf-fix-latency-tool` (by EPAM, GitHub)** – *Closest to Corvil’s FIX latency monitoring*\n  * **What it does:** Attaches eBPF TC hooks at the Linux kernel level to inspect TCP payloads, extracts **FIX Tag 11 (`ClOrdID`)**, correlates inbound requests with outbound responses, and computes round-trip latency with **nanosecond precision**.\n  * **Why it’s great:** Outputs HDR histograms (`p50`, `p99`, `p99.999`) in real time and has been validated up to ~500,000 FIX messages/sec with very low overhead.\n  * **Limitation:** Only monitors FIX Tag 11 on the host where it runs (not an out-of-band network tap appliance).\n\n* **`pcap_latency_analyzer` (by FMADIO, GitHub)** – *Closest to Corvil’s wire-to-wire hop latency*\n  * **What it does:** Takes hardware-timestamped PCAPs captured at two points (e.g., switch ingress and egress, or two redundant market data feeds), hashes the TCP/UDP payloads, matches identical packets, and generates a nanosecond-resolution latency histogram.\n  * **Limitation:** Post-capture CLI analysis tool rather than a live web dashboard.\n\n---\n\n### 2. For Deep Packet Inspection (DPI) \u0026 Protocol Decoding\nIf you need Corvil’s ability to passively decode wire protocols (including custom or financial protocols) into structured logs/metrics:\n\n* **Zeek + Spicy (BSD License)** – *Closest to Corvil’s wire-data decoding engine*\n  * **What it does:** Passively inspects live traffic (via SPAN/TAP) and transforms raw packets into rich, structured transaction logs (TCP connection metrics, RTT, HTTP, TLS, DNS, etc.).\n  * **Financial / Custom Protocols:** Zeek natively includes **Spicy** (a parser generator), which financial firms use to write custom dissectors—such as for **FIX** (4.0–5.0/FIXT) or binary market data feeds—without having to store petabytes of raw PCAPs.\n  * **Best paired with:** OpenSearch/ClickHouse + Grafana for dashboards and alerting.\n\n---\n\n### 3. For High-Speed Full Packet Capture \u0026 Search\nIf you want Corvil’s continuous \"always-on\" PCAP recording with fast querying:\n\n* **Arkime (formerly Moloch, Apache 2.0 License)**\n  * **What it does:** Captures traffic at tens of Gbps to disk in standard PCAP format while indexing L3–L7 session metadata into OpenSearch/Elasticsearch. You get a web UI to search sessions by IP, port, protocol, or tags, and export exact PCAP slices directly into **Wireshark** (which itself has built-in dissectors for FIX, ITCH, OUCH, etc.).\n  * **Note on precision:** For sub-microsecond timestamps, pair Linux capture tools (`netsniff-ng` or `tcpdump --time-stamp-precision\u003dnano`) with a PTP-synchronized NIC (`linuxptp`).\n\n---\n\n### 4. For Real-Time Network Performance, RTT \u0026 Burst Visibility\nIf you are using Corvil more as a general **Network Performance Monitoring \u0026 Diagnostics (NPMD)** tool rather than for trading protocols:\n\n* **ntopng Community Edition + nDPI (GPLv3)**\n  * **What it does:** Continuous real-time traffic visibility, Deep Packet Inspection (via nDPI), TCP retransmissions, packet loss, and RTT/latency KPIs. Newer versions also support high-resolution time-series (15-second granularity or lower) to catch short traffic spikes.\n  * **Caveat:** The core `ntopng` Community edition is free and open source, while their high-speed 100G disk-recording module (`n2disk`) and zero-copy drivers (`PF_RING ZC`) require paid licenses.\n\n* **DeepFlow (Apache 2.0 License)**\n  * **What it does:** Uses eBPF on Linux servers/Kubernetes to automatically build a service map and measure per-flow **TCP connection latency, ACK delay, and application response latency** with zero code changes. It also supports **Wasm plugins** if you want to parse proprietary protocols.\n  * **Best for:** Cloud-native, microservice, or Linux host environments rather than hardware switch taps.\n\n* **Elastic Packetbeat (Open Source / Elastic License)**\n  * **What it does:** Lightweight packet shipper that calculates request/response latency for standard protocols (HTTP, DNS, TLS, MySQL, PostgreSQL, Redis) and streams them into Elasticsearch/OpenSearch + Kibana.\n\n---\n\n### Summary: How to Build a \"DIY Corvil\" Stack for Free\nIf you want to assemble an end-to-end free alternative on commodity Linux hardware:\n\n| Corvil Feature | Open-Source Equivalent |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Hardware Timestamping** | PTP-capable NIC (e.g., NVIDIA ConnectX / Intel) + **`linuxptp`** |\n| **Lossless Full PCAP \u0026 Search** | **`Arkime`** (or **`netsniff-ng`** for raw capture) |\n| **Protocol Decoding (incl. FIX)** | **`Zeek` + `Spicy`** (or **`epam/ebpf-fix-latency-tool`** for FIX RTT) |\n| **Real-time Flow \u0026 TCP Health** | **`ntopng Community`** or **`DeepFlow`** |\n| **Storage \u0026 Dashboards** | **ClickHouse** or **OpenSearch** + **Grafana** |\n\nIf you let me know whether your priority is **financial/trading protocols (FIX, market data gaps, tick-to-trade)** or **general data center network latency and microbursts**, I can narrow this down to a specific setup guide.",
