      "parts": [{
        "text": "There is **no single 1:1 open"
      }, {
        "text": "-source drop-in replacement** for Pico’s Corvil Analytics."
      }, {
        "text": " Corvil is a highly specialized platform that combines hardware-accelerated nanosecond timestamping, lossless high-speed packet capture (up"
      }, {
        "text": " to 200 Gbps), built-in decoders for financial protocols (FIX, ITCH, OUCH, SBE),"
      }, {
        "text": " microburst detection, and multi-hop trade lifecycle correlation"
      }, {
        "text": ".\n\nHowever, depending on **which part of Corvil** you are trying to replicate, you can get very"
      }, {
        "text": " close using specialized open-source tools—or by combining a few of them into a stack.\n\n---\n\n### "
      }, {
        "text": "1. For Financial Protocol (FIX) \u0026 Nanosecond Latency Tracking\nIf you want Corvil’s core trading/HFT latency analytics"
      }, {
        "text": " (measuring order-to-ack delays and hop-by-hop network latency), look at these specialized open-source tools:\n\n* **"
      }, {
        "text": "`ebpf-fix-latency-tool` (by EPAM, GitHub)** – *Closest to Corvil’s FIX"
      }, {
        "text": " latency monitoring*\n  * **What it does:** Attaches eBPF TC hooks at the Linux kernel level"
      }, {
        "text": " to inspect TCP payloads, extracts **FIX Tag 11 (`ClOrdID`)**, correlates inbound requests with outbound responses, and computes round-"
      }, {
        "text": "trip latency with **nanosecond precision**.\n  "
      }, {
        "text": "* **Why it’s great:** Outputs HDR histograms (`p50`, `p99`, `p9"
      }, {
        "text": "9.999`) in real time and has been validated up to ~500,000 FIX messages/sec with very low overhead"
      }, {
        "text": ".\n  * **Limitation:** Only monitors FIX Tag 11 on the host where"
      }, {
        "text": " it runs (not an out-of-band network tap appliance).\n\n* **`pcap_latency_analyzer"
      }, {
        "text": "` (by FMADIO, GitHub)** – *Closest to Corvil’s wire-to-wire hop latency"
      }, {
        "text": "*\n  * **What it does:** Takes hardware-timestamped PCAPs captured at"
      }, {
        "text": " two points (e.g., switch ingress and egress, or two redundant market data feeds), hashes the TCP/UDP payloads, matches"
      }, {
        "text": " identical packets, and generates a nanosecond-resolution latency histogram.\n"
      }, {
        "text": "  * **Limitation:** Post-capture CLI analysis tool rather than a live web dashboard"
      }, {
        "text": ".\n\n---\n\n### 2. For Deep Packet Inspection (DPI) \u0026 Protocol Decoding\nIf you need Corvil’s ability to passively decode wire"
      }, {
        "text": " protocols (including custom or financial protocols) into structured logs/metrics:\n\n* **Zeek + Spicy (BSD License)** – *Closest to Corvil"
      }, {
        "text": "’s wire-data decoding engine*\n  * **"
      }, {
        "text": "What it does:** Passively inspects live traffic (via SPAN/TAP) and transforms raw packets into rich, structured transaction logs ("
      }, {
        "text": "TCP connection metrics, RTT, HTTP, TLS, DNS, etc.)"
      }, {
        "text": ".\n  * **Financial / Custom Protocols:** Zeek natively includes **Spicy** (a parser generator),"
      }, {
        "text": " which financial firms use to write custom dissectors—such as for **FIX** (4.0–5.0/"
      }, {
        "text": "FIXT) or binary market data feeds—without having to store petabytes of raw PCAPs"
      }, {
        "text": ".\n  * **Best paired with:** OpenSearch/ClickHouse + Grafana for dashboards and alerting.\n\n---\n\n###"
      }, {
        "text": " 3. For High-Speed Full Packet Capture \u0026 Search\nIf you want Corvil’s continuous \"always-on\" PCAP recording with"
      }, {
        "text": " fast querying:\n\n* **Arkime (formerly Moloch, Apache 2.0 License"
      }, {
        "text": ")**\n  * **What it does:** Captures traffic at tens of Gbps to disk in"
      }, {
        "text": " standard PCAP format while indexing L3–L7 session metadata into OpenSearch/Elasticsearch"
      }, {
        "text": ". You get a web UI to search sessions by IP, port, protocol, or tags, and export exact PCAP slices"
      }, {
        "text": " directly into **Wireshark** (which itself has built-in dissectors for FIX, ITCH, OUCH, etc.).\n  * **Note on precision:** For sub-microsecond timestamps,"
      }, {
        "text": " pair Linux capture tools (`netsniff-ng` or `tcpdump --time-stamp-precision\u003dnano`)"
      }, {
        "text": " with a PTP-synchronized NIC (`linuxptp`).\n\n---\n\n### 4."
      }, {
        "text": " For Real-Time Network Performance, RTT \u0026 Burst Visibility\nIf you are using Corvil more as a general **Network Performance Monitoring \u0026 Diagnostics"
      }, {
        "text": " (NPMD)** tool rather than for trading protocols:\n\n* **ntopng Community Edition + nDPI (GPL"
      }, {
        "text": "v3)**\n  * **What it does"
      }, {
        "text": ":** Continuous real-time traffic visibility, Deep Packet Inspection (via nDPI), TCP retransmissions, packet loss, and"
      }, {
        "text": " RTT/latency KPIs. Newer versions also support high-resolution time"
      }, {
        "text": "-series (15-second granularity or lower) to catch short traffic spikes.\n  * **Caveat:** The"
      }, {
        "text": " core `ntopng` Community edition is free and open source, while their high-speed 100G"
      }, {
        "text": " disk-recording module (`n2disk`) and zero-copy drivers (`PF_RING ZC`) require paid licenses"
      }, {
        "text": ".\n\n* **DeepFlow (Apache 2.0 License)**\n  "
      }, {
